{"availability":"available","full":"jaykesner/directchat","name":"directchat","description":"Chat app made with React and Firebase.","category":"Developer tools","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2021-06-24T15:45:13Z","updated":"2023-03-31T15:08:38Z","branch":"develop","homepage":"https://directchat.netlify.app/","topics":["cloudfirestore","firebase","mantine","netlify","react","reactrouter"],"demo":"https://directchat.netlify.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T20:11:40.457Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T20:11:40.457Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T20:11:40.457Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T20:11:40.457Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Chat app made with Create React App and Firebase, deployed automatically from github commits to Netlify.","Direct Chat is a chat app that uses React for the frontend and Cloud Firestore from Firebase for the backend. This allows the app to have chat rooms, each having a five digit id that be accessed or shared directly by adding the id to the end of the url (ex. directchat.netlify.app/XY1B2). The app has no sign in or user accounts, users can create a username on the fly which is stored in the session.","My goals for this project were to create a sensibly scoped React project that I can \"finish\" and continue to iterate on, which includes routing, APIs, async/await, and CI/CD. Firestore is a great piece of tech for this because it's both an API and a backend, which led me to learning some things about cloud database security as well."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jaykesner/directchat/blob/develop/README.md","fingerprint":"8ce490b4cf58dfbf308bd8ec865f2164a7a364774dea2a5322d4d1ee2fbfbf3a","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T20:11:40.566Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T20:11:40.566Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Chat app made with Create React App and Firebase, deployed automatic